This folder contains tests and test results for testing all the library specification files.

The SpecsBase suite tests each specification .jml file
-- output of the test is in <classname>-actual
-- output is compared against <classname>-expected or the output is presumed to be empty if there is no such expected file

SpecsEsc and SpecsRac use the custom test method that is in the folder for the given class.
The folder name is the classname with '.' characters replaced by '-' characters
The folder contains one (arbitrarily named) .java file.
In the SpecsEsc test suite, openjml --esc is run on this .java file and the output put in 'actual', which is expected to match 'expected'.
  The esc proof attempt excludes the main method and constructor of the test file.
In the SpecsRac test suite, openjml --rac is run on this .java file and the output put in 'actual-compile', which is expected to match 'expected-compile'
  If the --rac compilation is successful, the compiled program is executed (using openjml-java) and the output put in 'actual-run', 
  which is expected to match 'expected-run'.